ophrenia. It refers to which of the following?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Psychiatry","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Visual splitting"},{"label":"B","text":"Oriented to time but not place and person"},{"label":"C","text":"Having delusional orientation separate from reality"},{"label":"D","text":"Intermingled delusional and real life orientation"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Psychiatry","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ab23bc990fe4","stem":"Your pharmacist has asked you to reduce or change antipsychotic prescriptions to an inpatient as he has developed akathisia. Akathisia refers to which of the following descriptions?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","topicOriginal":"Central Nervous System Drugs","subtopic":"Antipsychotic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Poor attention span"},{"label":"B","text":"Recurrent violent impulses"},{"label":"C","text":"Restlessness without autonomic features"},{"label":"D","text":"Anxiety characterized by cognitive and somatic features"},{"label":"E","text":"Fidgety, shuffling gait"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ea2885ad647f","stem":"Which of the following is not a catatonic symptom?","type":"Single