g time for Tanzania’s population Knowing where people move to eg refuges Moving to towns, seasonal agricultural migration Moshi town and migration Fertility rates: Total fertility rate (TFR). The average number of children that would be born alive to a woman during her lifetime if she experiences the current age specific fertility rate. As of 2020 Tanzania 4.8 change rate of – 1.22 As of 2010 was 5.4 alive children. [Slide 10] population health? See the wordomenter!!! Population."},{"label":"A","text":"Measuring the population"},{"label":"B","text":"Describing the structure of a population (The cupboard 3 X 3)."},{"label":"C","text":"Population growth TZ 2.9%"},{"label":"D","text":"Trending of the world and Africa population."},{"label":"E","text":"Population Policies"},{"label":"F","text":"Call for Holistic Population Health Perspective."}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","duplicate_option_text","long_option_manual_review","nonunique_option_labels","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-634c852c27ab","stem":"67 percent of world population For every 151 people one is a Tanzanian Estimated to have nearly 60 million people and worldometer as 30th June, 2022 is appr 63,347,189 mil Tanzania population growth rate of 2.9 per year High fertility among 15 – 19 year old persons 1960 was 10.5 mil to 59.73 mil in 2020. increase of 494.2 in 60 years. Total world population increased by 156 % in the same period. 35% of the people live in towns [Slide 11] populati